  "body": "Supersedes #42 \u2014 its commit is preserved in this branch's history, so merging this lands both. Close #42 without merging.\n\n## What changed and why\n\n### Coverage stops blocking games\n\n`coverage.rules.percent must be 100` is gone from `intake-lib.mjs`. A candidate now enters with whatever it can evidence, and later passes add to it. Rules coverage stays the working aim; components and other factual detail may land low-to-mid.\n\nWhat remains is the honesty of the ledger, and that got stricter in intent if not in code \u2014 the existing arithmetic checks are now the *point* of the ledger rather than a side condition: a count may not exceed its denominator, a percentage must be the computed result, an unretrieved denominator stays `null`. Admission rests entirely on claim-level `Source / Evidence / Confidence` support.\n\nA packet may now carry open `followups`. Forbidding them pressured a worker to leave a known gap unrecorded, which is backwards \u2014 they are the additive to-do the weekly librarian already drains.\n\n### The Elder Sign deadlock\n\n`intakeCompletionGateFindings` no longer arms on the PR view (`--synthetic-merge`), only at merge time (`--require-merge-commit`).\n\nThe old gate demanded a `promoted` head on every open intake PR. Only the auditor can author the `approval.json` that promotion requires, so no scout action could ever clear it \u2014 #38 was told twice to \"restore green CI\" for a state only its auditor could produce. Verified against the real stuck packet:\n\n- PR view on `kb/intake-elder-sign` merged into this branch: `validate-intake: clean`\n- Same head under `--require-merge-commit`: still refuses the unpromoted intake\n\nProtected `main` is unchanged: an intake still cannot reach it unpromoted.\n\n### Unattended operation\n\nEvery procedure that named a person now names a document. Followups and `intake-gap` leads must name something a later scheduled run can actually fetch, because nothing waits on a reply. Both operator profiles gain an explicit unattended section: what each may do without asking, what has no override, and what to do with a question that used to be escalated (record it and decide).\n\nThe auditor's profile also gains the rule that #38 violated \u2014 a `REVISE` must name a defect a scout context can actually repair \u2014 and a line that an auto-merge setting is not an audit.\n\nProvenance is preserved: dated instructions in `operations.okf.md` keep their records under a neutral operator label rather than being deleted. New `src-012` records this change.\n\n### Visual contract\n\n`OKF_SPEC.md` now defines \"private\" as this repository and its private sync targets. The same packet was approved under one reading on 08-01 and rejected under the other on 08-03, against 93 `editorial-excerpt` references already in the corpus. Includes the standing consequence: if the repo ever goes public, that is a corpus-wide visual re-basing, not a per-packet call.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node --test` intake suite: 45 pass, 0 fail, 1 intentional skip\n- `node --test scripts/validate-okf-visuals.test.mjs`: 0 fail\n- `node scripts/validate-okf.mjs`: 2637 files clean + INDEX fresh\n- `node scripts/validate-intake.mjs --base origin/main`: clean\n- `node .claude/hooks/okf-guard.mjs self-test`: green\n\n## Not addressed here\n\nLive `intake-gap` issues #23/#24 don't use the mandated title key (`[intake-gap]` + slug + bracketed BGG id), so the documented dedupe search can't match them. Cohort labels remain unenforced (Onirim, a solitaire game, occupies a `cooperative` slot). `.claude/commands/librarian.md` and `audit.md` still instruct a direct push to protected `main`. Each is separable from this change.",
